.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NQDCHK 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqdchk ,
.Nm nqdrepn ,
.Nm nqdrepi ,
.Nm nqdrepj ,
.Nm nqdrepfree
.Nd check a capsule's data record against its files
.Sh LIBRARY
libnqd, \-lnqd \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nqd.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqdchk "const char *dir" "nqdrep **rep"
.Ft size_t
.Fn nqdrepn "const nqdrep *r"
.Ft int
.Fo nqdrepi
.Fa "const nqdrep *r" "size_t i"
.Fa "const char **check" "int *ok" "const char **detail"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fn nqdrepj "const nqdrep *r" "size_t i"
.Ft void
.Fn nqdrepfree "nqdrep *r"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqdchk
reads
.Pa noqtis.data.json
in
.Fa dir
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5
and checks the folder against it, one report row per check:
.Bl -tag -width recorded
.It Ql record
the record reads, is of the format and canonical (the detail says
what is wrong when not)
.It Ql source
one per source: its file is there, with the recorded SHA-256 (compared
in constant time) and size
.It Ql schema , Ql rule
one per schema: its file matches the columns, types, missing-value
codes, ranges and sets; one per rule
.It Ql stats
one per summary: made again from its file, read as the element says
.Pq Cm delim , Cm header ,
else as the file's schema says, the summaries are the recorded ones
byte for byte (a calibration,
.Cm cal ,
aside); the detail names the first column that differs
.It Ql step
one per step with both
.Cm script
and
.Cm sha256 :
the script or mapping is in the folder with that SHA-256
.It Ql recorded
one per recorded check: it fails when the check was recorded as
.Ql fail .
When
.Cm expected
and
.Cm observed
are both numbers it is recomputed:
.Ql |observed - expected| <= tol
.Pq Cm tol No 0 when not given ;
when both are strings, they must be equal.
A check recorded as
.Ql pass
that does not hold fails; the detail gives the numbers
.El
.Pp
A row about a file marked
.Cm synthetic
says
.Ql [synthetic]
after the path.
It checks nothing of the seal: check the capsule with
.Xr nqchk 3
too.
.Pp
.Fn nqdrepn ,
.Fn nqdrepi
and
.Fn nqdrepfree
read and free the report as
.Xr nqrep 3
does a capsule's.
.Fn nqdrepj
returns the numbers of row
.Fa i
as canonical JSON, for rows that have them (those of
.Xr nqddrift 3 ) ,
or
.Dv NULL .
The strings stay valid until the report is freed.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn nqdchk
returns
.Dv NQOK
when every row passed and
.Dv NQEVRFY
when one failed (no record, or one that does not read, is a failed
.Ql record
row); in both cases
.Fa *rep
is set.
.Dv NQEARG
and
.Dv NQEMEM
return no report.
.Fn nqdrepi
returns
.Dv NQEARG
for a row that is not there.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-data 1 ,
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqdnew 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
